            <div xml:id="d335">

                <pb facs="0488" n="400" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg400"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/12581: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sharp</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-23T18:00:00+00:00"
                            >December 23, 1918—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 23—5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6447. Reference your 6723, December 21, 7 p.m.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d335-f1"/>
                    When telegraphing to the Department joint telegrams from the Allied Ministers at
                    Jassy, this Embassy has automatically sent copies to the American Mission. This
                    custom has also been followed with all telegrams and other communications
                    containing information which is thought to be of interest to the Mission. See my
                    6144, December 5, 7 p.m.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d335-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sharp</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
